{
  "message": "Thank you for providing your information, John. To help diagnose why your phone is showing 'No Service,' could you please check your phone's status bar and let me know what icons or messages you see at the top of your screen? This will help me determine if Airplane Mode is on or if there are any signal indicators."
}

{
  "message": "The airplane icon means that Airplane Mode is currently enabled on your phone. When Airplane Mode is on, all wireless connections—including cellular service—are turned off, which is why you see 'No Service.'\n\nPlease turn off Airplane Mode on your phone. You can usually do this by swiping down from the top of your screen to open the quick settings panel and tapping the airplane icon to disable it. Once Airplane Mode is off, let me know if your service returns or if you still see 'No Service.'"
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for turning off Airplane Mode. Since your phone still shows 'No Signal,' the next step is to check if your SIM card is being recognized by your phone. Please check your SIM card status on your device and let me know if it shows as active, missing, or locked. This will help us determine if the issue is with the SIM card itself."
}

{
  "message": "If your phone says there’s no SIM card detected, it means your phone cannot find the SIM card that connects you to the cellular network. This is a common cause of 'No Service.'\n\nPlease try removing your SIM card and then reinserting it to make sure it is seated properly. After you do this, check if your phone recognizes the SIM card and if your service returns. Let me know what happens after you reseat the SIM card."
}

